        "evidence": "quantum-su2.md:1 declares q∈ℂ* with 0<|q|≤1 (archimedean, complex). quantum-su2.lean:30 sets R_q=LaurentPolynomial ℤ and q_ne_one (formal indeterminate, no |q|≤1 / 0<q expressible). The regime '0<|q|≤1' from the narrative is not represented; also qInt uses division in R_q (a non-field) — qInt_two relies on q−1≠0 but R_q=ℤ[q,q⁻¹] is not a field, so (qⁿ−1)/(q−1) is only well-defined as a Laurent polynomial when the division is exact (it is, but the `/` is the GroupWithZero/junk-division on a non-field).",
